{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"001-redshelf-66","prompting_method_id":"shophouse-design-concept-revise.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"redshelf-66-envelope.v1"},"style":{"name":"Yellow Terracotta Twin-Gable Shophouse","rationale":"Warm yellow terracotta merchant's house read as two shops. A proud terracotta pier at x5-6 and stripped dark-oak corner posts frame two shopfronts set back 2 cells (glass, stall-risers and doors at z2), leaving covered porches under striped wool awnings at z0-1. Orange/white marks the left shop and blue/white the right, and each has a hanging sign and a lantern. A continuous dark-oak floor beam at y5 wraps the front, right side and back. The upper windows are recessed 1 cell, with glass at the inner plane, flower pots resting on the beam and closed top-trapdoor hoods. They are flanked by open trapdoor shutters whose facing is the outward normal, so each panel sits on the inner edge of its cell over a terracotta backing and reads as a recessed panel. For that reason the right-side shutters face east, not west as the document said. An upside-down stone-brick stair cornice at y9 runs on the front, right and back for a corbel shadow line without crossing the lot line. Each shop has its own steep mud-brick gable with its ridge front to back: stair courses at y10/y11, a mud-brick ridge at y12 and a slab cap at y13. The two roofs meet in a stair valley at x5/x6. Each gable end is terracotta with a deep-set attic window. The x0 party wall stays plain, and the back repeats the front's upper storey with recessed back doors."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:yellow_terracotta","minecraft:mud_bricks","minecraft:mud_brick_stairs","minecraft:mud_brick_slab","minecraft:stripped_dark_oak_log","minecraft:dark_oak_planks","minecraft:dark_oak_door","minecraft:dark_oak_trapdoor","minecraft:stone_brick_stairs","minecraft:orange_wool","minecraft:white_wool","minecraft:blue_wool","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraf